Name: systemAppearanceChanged

Type: message

Syntax: systemAppearanceChanged

Summary:
Sent to the <current card> of the <defaultStack> when the <systemAppearance>
changes.

Associations: card

Introduced: 1.0

OS: mac, windows, linux, android, html5

Platforms: desktop,mobile

Example:
on systemAppearanceChanged
    if the systemAppearance is "dark" then
        set the backColor of me to "black"
        set the foreColor of me to "white"
    else
        set the backColor of me to "white"
        set the foreColor of me to "black"
    end if
end systemAppearanceChanged

Description:
Handle the <systemAppearanceChanged> <message> if you need to change the color
of objects when the application enters either light or dark mode.

On Linux the message is sent when the desktop's GTK theme changes, which is
how a desktop switches between light and dark there; the <systemAppearance>
itself reports "light" on Linux, so a handler can compare the
<effective> <backgroundColor> of a stack to tell a dark theme from a light
one. While the <useDesktopAppearance> is true, the <systemAppearance>
follows the desktop's light or dark setting instead, and the message is
also sent when GNOME's "color-scheme" setting switches it, and when setting
the <useDesktopAppearance> changes it.

The message is sent once, to the <current card> of the <defaultStack>.
In the development environment the <defaultStack> is often one of its own
stacks; then the message is also sent to the <current card> of the
frontmost open stack that is not part of the development environment and
whose card, stack or main stack (or one of their behaviors) has a
<systemAppearanceChanged> handler. A handler in a library or a backscript
gets the message wherever it is sent.

In an HTML5 standalone the message is sent when the browser's colour scheme
changes, on a page built with **Appearance** set to **Follow the browser**
in the Web pane of the Standalone Application Settings.

References: systemAppearance (property), message (glossary), defaultStack (property),
current card (glossary), effective (keyword), backgroundColor (property),
useDesktopAppearance (property)

